  "worked_solution": "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\u230ax\u230b$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n\u230ax\u230b=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=1.5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.5) & ={e}^{\u230a8/1.5\u230b} \\\\  & ={e}^{\u230a5.333\u2026\u230b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\u230a5.333\u2026\u230b=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.5) & ={e}^{\u230a5.333\u2026\u230b} \\\\  & ={e}^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
